px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"world pet names\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose prose-lg max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"📋 Table of Contents\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gradient-to-br from-primary/5 to-indigo-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/10 mb-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\",\"children\":\"📋 Table of Contents\"}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 list-none pl-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[1,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#intro\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Introduction: Names as Cultural Windows\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[2,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#japan\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Japanese Pet Naming Traditions\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[3,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#nordic\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Nordic & Viking Naming Traditions\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[4,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#india\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Indian & South Asian Pet Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[5,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#africa\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"African Naming Traditions for Animals\"}]]}],\"$La\",\"$Lb\",\"$Lc\"]}]]}],\"$Ld\",\"$Le\",\"$Lf\",\"$L10\",\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\",\"$L15\",\"$L16\",\"$L17\",\"$L18\",\"$L19\",\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\",\"$L1d\",\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\",\"$L21\",\"$L22\",\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\",\"$L26\"]}],\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\"]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$2e\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@2f\"}]}]\na:[\"$\",\"li\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[6,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#latin\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Latin American Pet Naming Customs\"}]]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"li\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[7,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#europe\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Western European Pet Naming Patterns\"}]]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"li\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[8,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#faq\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\"}]]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Names as Cultural Windows\"]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Pet names are cultural artifacts. They reveal what a society values — its relationship with nature, its sense of humor, its spiritual beliefs, and its social structures. A Japanese pet name like 'Maru' (circle, symbolizing harmony and completeness) tells a different story than an American name like 'Rex' (king, reflecting individual dominance) or a Brazilian name like 'Caramelo' (caramel, evoking warmth and sweetness). Understanding these cultural dimensions enriches our appreciation of pet naming and may inspire your own choices.\"]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"At BestAnimalNames.com, we believe that exploring global naming traditions makes us better pet owners. It expands our creative palette and deepens our understanding of the human-animal bond across cultures.\"]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Japanese Pet Naming Traditions\"]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Japanese pet naming reflects the culture's deep appreciation for nature, cuteness (kawaii), and linguistic playfulness. Traditional Japanese pet names often draw from: natural phenomena — Hana (flower), Yuki (snow), Sora (sky), Kumo (cloud); food — Mochi, Mikan (tangerine), Azuki (red bean), Kinako; doubled syllables — Momo (peach), Kiki, Fufu, Mimi, which sound affectionate; and honorifics — adding '-chan' or '-kun' to names (Taro-kun, Hana-chan) for endearment.\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Japanese pet naming is also deeply influenced by the Buddhist concept of 'ichigo ichie' — treasuring each encounter as unique. This philosophy encourages pet owners to choose names that honor the singular nature of their relationship with their animal. Names may reference the season or circumstances of the first meeting — Aki (autumn) for a pet adopted in fall, or Nagi (calm) for a pet that brought peace during a turbulent time.\"]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"p\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Modern Japanese pet names increasingly blend traditional values with global influences. Top names in Tokyo pet registries include: Sora, Mugi (barley), Leo, Coco, Maron (chestnut), and Kotetsu (small iron — for tough little pets). The influence of anime and manga has also created a wave of fandom-inspired names.\"]}]\n14:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Nordic & Viking Naming Traditions\"]}]\n15:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Nordic pet naming draws from a rich heritage of Norse mythology, Viking history, and connection to dramatic natural landscapes. Scandinavian names for pets often carry powerful, elemental meanings: mythological names — Thor, Odin, Freya, Loki, Saga, Balder; nature names — Bjørn (bear), Ulv (wolf), Sten (stone), Fjord, Vind (wind); and virtue names — Modig (brave), Stærk (strong), Klog (wise), inspired by Viking ideals.\"]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"p\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"In Iceland, naming traditions are particularly distinctive. Icelandic pets often receive names from the sagas — ancient medieval texts that form the core of Icelandic cultural identity. A dog might be named 'Skarpur' (sharp, clever) from Njáls Saga, or a cat 'Freyja' after the goddess of love. Iceland's strict naming laws for humans do not apply to pets, giving owners creative freedom they do not have for their children.\"]}]\n17:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Swedish and Danish pet names often reflect the 'lagom' philosophy — not too much, not too little, just right. Names like Lagom, Mysig (cozy), and Fika (coffee break — a cherished Swedish ritual) reflect cultural values of balance, comfort, and simple pleasures.\"]}]\n18:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Indian & South Asian Pet Names\"]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"p\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Indian pet naming traditions are intensely diverse, reflecting the subcontinent's multitude of languages, religions, and cultural practices. Common themes include: Sanskrit-derived names — Shakti (power), Devi (goddess), Raja (king), Sundar (beautiful); Bollywood-inspired names — Raj, Simran, Prem; food names — Chai, Jalebi, Gulab, Paneer; and nature names — Nadi (river), Phool (flower), Surya (sun).\"]}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Hindu mythology provides an especially rich source of pet names. Hanuman (the monkey god) is a popular name for agile dogs. Ganesha (the elephant-headed god of wisdom) is often given to large, calm pets. Lakshmi (goddess of prosperity) is chosen for pets that bring good fortune. These names carry deep spiritual resonance and are chosen with reverence.\"]}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"In Muslim communities across South Asia, Arabic-origin names are common: Noor (light), Sultan (ruler), Amir (prince), and Yasmin (jasmine flower). Sikh families may choose names from the Guru Granth Sahib. This diversity means that Indian pet names offer one of the richest naming vocabularies in the world.\"]}]\n1c:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"17\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"African Naming Traditions for Animals\"]}]\n1d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"18\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Africa's 54 countries and thousands of ethnic groups produce an extraordinary diversity of pet naming traditions. Across the continent, names often carry specific meanings tied to: circumstances of the animal's arrival, physical characteristics, aspirational qualities, and ancestral connections.\"]}]\n1e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"19\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"In Swahili-speaking East Africa, names like Simba (lion), Tembo (elephant), Duma (cheetah), and Rafiki (friend) are beloved pet names. Zulu names from South Africa include Thando (love), Sipho (gift), and Nomvula (mother of rain — for pets that arrived during rainy season). Yoruba names from Nigeria like Oluwa (God/divine) and Ayo (joy) carry spiritual weight. Wolof names from Senegal — including Bouba (big, for large pets) and Yaye (mother, for nurturing female pets) — reflect daily life and social relationships.\"]}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"20\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Latin American Pet Naming Customs\"]}]\n20:[\"$\",\"p\",\"21\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Latin American pet naming blends indigenous naming traditions with Spanish and Portuguese colonial influences, creating vibrant, affectionate naming patterns. Common across the region: diminutives are extremely popular — adding '-ito' or '-ita' to any name expresses affection (Perrito, Gatita, Negrito); color-based names — Negro, Blanco, Canela (cinnamon), Ceniza (ash), Dorado (golden); food names — Taco, Churro, Pancho, Mantequilla (butter), Café; and soccer-inspired names — Messi, Pelé, Neymar, for athletic or competitive pets.\"]}]\n21:[\"$\",\"p\",\"22\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"In Brazil, Portuguese-influenced naming shows creativity and humor: Pipoca (popcorn), Feijão (bean), Brigadeiro (chocolate candy), and Soneca (nap — for sleepy pets). In Mexico, pre-Hispanic names are experiencing a revival: Xóchitl (flower), Cuauhtémoc (descending eagle), and Citlali (star) are increasingly popular for pets, reflecting cultural pride.\"]}]\n22:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"23\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Western European Pet Naming Patterns\"]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"p\",\"24\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Western Europe shows distinct national patterns despite geographic proximity. French names emphasize elegance and food — Coco, Chanel, Croissant, Baguette. German names favor strength and nature — Adler (eagle), Blitz (lightning), Bär (bear), Sturm (storm). Italian names celebrate beauty and passion — Bella, Amore, Tesoro, Dolce. British names lean toward the traditional and literary — Winston, Dickens, Pippin, Basil. These patterns persist even in immigrant communities, forming enduring cultural markers.\"]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"p\",\"25\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"The most striking trend across all cultures is the universal human impulse to name our animal companions with care and meaning. Whether a Norwegian dog named Thor, a Japanese cat named Yuki, or a Brazilian bird named Pipoca, pet names are declarations of love that transcend linguistic and cultural boundaries.\"]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"p\",\"26\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Explore our name generators for \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"32\",{\"href\":\"/animal/american-bullfrog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"American Bullfrog\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"53\",{\"href\":\"/animal/alligator-gar/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Alligator Gar\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"70\",{\"href\":\"/animal/anthias/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Anthias\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"81\",{\"href\":\"/animal/andean-cock-of-the-rock/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Andean Cock-of-the-Rock\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"112\",{\"href\":\"/animal/african-golden-wolf/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"African Golden Wolf\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" to find the perfect name for your companion.\"]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"27\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Frequently Asked Questions\"]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Is it cultural appropriation to use names from other cultures?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Using names from other cultures is generally fine when done with respect and understanding. Learn the meaning and context of the name you choose, and avoid names with sacred religious significance unless you belong to that tradition.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What is the most universal pet naming tradition?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Food names appear across virtually every culture — from Mochi in Japan to Churro in Mexico to Biscuit in England. Naming pets after beloved foods is a near-universal human practice.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I learn the correct pronunciation of a cultural name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Online pronunciation guides, YouTube videos by native speakers, and language-learning apps can help. Most people appreciate the effort to pronounce names correctly, even if your accent isn't perfect.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can I mix naming traditions?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Absolutely. Many multicultural families blend traditions beautifully. A dog might have a Spanish first name and a Japanese middle name. Your pet's name should reflect YOUR story, which may span multiple cultures.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are there any universal taboos in pet naming across cultures?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Most cultures avoid naming pets after revered religious figures, deceased family members (without permission), or offensive terms. Beyond that, taboos vary widely by region and community.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"lemur\",{\"href\":\"/animal/lemur/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐒\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Lemur\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"sugar-glider\",{\"href\":\"/animal/sugar-glider/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐿️\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Sugar Glider\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"cuban-crocodile\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cuban-crocodile/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐊\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Cuban Crocodile\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"long-eared-bat\",{\"href\":\"/animal/long-eared-bat/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦇\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Long-Eared Bat\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"lungfish\",{\"href\":\"/animal/lungfish/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐟\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Lungfish\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"sky-terrier\",{\"href\":\"/animal/sky-terrier/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐕\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Skye Terrier\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"pangolin\",{\"href\":\"/animal/pangolin/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦔\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Pangolin\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"black-backed-jackal\",{\"href\":\"/animal/black-backed-jackal/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐺\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Black-Backed Jackal\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n29:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"📖 Related Naming Guides\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"popular-cat-names\",{\"href\":\"/guide/popular-cat-names/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl\",\"children\":\"📖\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Popular Cat Names — Top Popular Picks 🐱\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"funny-dogs-names\",{\"href\":\"/guide/funny-dogs-names/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl\",\"children\":\"📖\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Funny Dogs Names — 100+ Ideas 💫\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"classic-hamster-names\",{\"href\":\"/guide/classic-hamster-names/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl\",\"children\":\"📖\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Classic Hamster Names — Top Classic Picks 🐹\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"popular-dog-names\",{\"href\":\"/guide/popular-dog-names/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl\",\"children\":\"📖\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Popular Dog Names — Top Popular Picks 🐕\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"📝 Related Articles\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"chinese-animal-names-symbolism-meaning\",{\"href\":\"/blog/chinese-animal-names-symbolism-meaning/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl mb-3\",\"children\":\"🐉\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Cultural Names\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mt-2 group-hover:text-primary line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Chinese Animal Names: Symbolism, Meaning & 200+ Beautiful Choices\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1 line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Discover the beauty of Chinese animal names and their deep cultural symbolism. From dragons to pandas, explore meaningful Chinese names perfect for pets with rich cultural heritage.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"unique-pet-names-from-around-world\",{\"href\":\"/blog/unique-pet-names-from-around-world/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl mb-3\",\"children\":\"🌍\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-primary/10 text-primary font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"Unique Names\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-bold text-gray-800 mt-2 group-hover:text-primary line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"120 Unique Pet Names from Around the World 🌍\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1 line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Discover 120 unique pet names inspired by cultures across the globe. From Japanese elegance to Scandinavian strength, find meaningful international names with beautiful origins and deep